{
  "about": "Maths a user types as plain text, as the phone draws it in the sent bubble and as the server reads it. The phone (apps/mobile/lib/math/__tests__/userMathsFixture.test.ts) turns each `text` into the markdown its bubble draws (lib/math/normalizeImplicit.ts) and expects `drawn`; the server (apps/api/app/tests/behavior/test_user_maths_fixture.py) reads the maths in `drawn` with its LaTeX path and `typed`, the words of `text` that hold it, with the parser a turn reads a message with, and holds both to one SymPy expression. A bracket glued to a name, a number or a caret groups an argument, a factor or an exponent, and keeps its meaning: \"ln(x^2 + 1)\" once drew as \"ln x² + 1\". A bracket set off by a space is only a delimiter. A glued run is one formula: a head and its scripts (x^2, log_2), consecutive brackets and a power (\"sin(x^2)cos(x^2)\" once broke into a display block).",
